.TH TEATHERD 1 "August 2026" "Teather 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
teatherd \- Teather per-user connection manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B teatherd
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B teatherd
owns phone detection and Teather connection state. It is normally activated on
the session bus and can optionally be enabled as a systemd user service for
login-time device watching. Only one phone can be active at a time.
.PP
On exit the daemon attempts to clean the exact ADB forward and tunnel resources
recorded in its mode-0600 ownership journal. Ambiguous resources are left in
place for explicit recovery rather than removed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR teather (1),
.BR teather-gtk (1)
